From 9dd6a06b27295c7014b064f0b022d2e9a2851f9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kudriavuy <169286443+kudriavuy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:31:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Animations: key highlight, Control Strip slide, slider
 growing

With Animations = true (off by default):
- a pressed key fades to ButtonActiveColor in 60 ms and back in 150 ms;
  only that key is redrawn;
- when Expand/Collapse changes the strip, the new row fades in while it
  slides 160 px into place and the old one fades out, 200 ms; Esc stays;
- a slider grows out of its button to SliderWidth in 150 ms, its contents
  and the round close button fading in while the row behind it fades
  out; closing (close button, a touch beside it, the timeout, the end of
  a slide) runs it backwards in 120 ms.
Keys are sent at once, never after an animation, and a new touch ends any
animation at once. While something moves the loop wakes every 16 ms (a
full frame takes about 11 ms on the T1); otherwise nothing changes. With
animations off the bar is drawn exactly as before.

The PNG preview shows frames of each animation, and the render timing a
frame of the strip transition.

Local patch for MacBookPro13,2 (T1), not from upstream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream: https://github.com/AsahiLinux/tiny-dfr (applies to 285faff8b8cae893e9babd673b904929dd6f7f9c)
